{"operations":[{"content":"\"\"\"chunking: split sequences into fixed-size chunks.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef chunk(items, size):\n    if size <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"size must be positive\")\n    if len(items) == 0:\n        return []\n    # If size is larger than input, return one chunk\n    if size >= len(items):\n        return [items]\n    # Otherwise, chunk normally, including final partial chunk\n    chunks = [items[i:i + size] for i in range(0, len(items), size)]\n    return chunks\n","expected_sha256":"7016a2b0dd284435e6f15970d4ba190d6386f23bccd03385aede97ee462ae675","kind":"modify","path":"src/chunking.py"}],"rationale":"Modified chunk function to include the final partial chunk when length is not a multiple of size, and to return one chunk if size is larger than input, preserving the public API and existing tests."}